WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.305
A relational table represents rows with defined attributes.

00:00:03.305 --> 00:00:09.502
A candidate key uniquely identifies a row; the chosen primary key is one candidate key.

00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:15.286
A foreign key links values to a referenced key and helps preserve referential integrity.

00:00:15.286 --> 00:00:17.765
Meaningful relationships should be expressed explicitly.

00:00:18.765 --> 00:00:23.159
Two students can share a name, and a name can change.

00:00:23.159 --> 00:00:27.554
A stable assigned identifier avoids confusing identity with a descriptive attribute.

00:00:27.554 --> 00:00:30.350
The identifier still needs a uniqueness constraint.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:35.556
Which rule prevents two students sharing the same primary-key value?

00:00:35.556 --> 00:00:38.500
A primary key identifies each row uniquely.
